::ENG3_U06_L05_GP01::MLA.ENG3.C.02
Context: A student is creating a digital presentation about how a historical setting affects a character's choices.
Which multimedia element would best improve audience understanding?{
~A. A decorative background pattern#Incorrect. A pattern may make the slide look full, but it does not clarify the setting or the character's choices.
=B. A labeled map showing where the main events occur#Correct. A map directly supports audience understanding by connecting place to the character's decisions. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. A random song that matches the student's mood#Incorrect. Music may create atmosphere, but if it does not clarify the analysis, it distracts from the purpose.
~D. A large animation on every slide#Incorrect. Repeated animation may distract the audience instead of improving understanding.
}

::ENG3_U06_L05_GP02::MLA.ENG3.C.02
Context: A presentation slide includes a chart, but the audience may not know why it matters.
What should the speaker add?{
~A. A brighter font color only#Incorrect. Color alone does not explain the chart's connection to the presentation claim. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. A second chart with no explanation#Incorrect. Adding more information without explanation can increase confusion. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. A longer title that repeats the same topic#Incorrect. A title helps, but it does not fully explain how the chart supports the point. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=D. A clear caption explaining the chart's connection to the claim#Correct. A caption helps the audience understand why the chart is included and how it supports the message. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
}

::ENG3_U06_L05_GP03::MLA.ENG3.C.02
Context: A student wants to include a photograph in a presentation about a text's setting.
Which question should guide the choice?{
=A. Will this image help the audience understand the setting or evidence?#Correct. Multimedia should be chosen because it improves understanding of the presentation's purpose. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~B. Is this the most colorful image I can find?#Incorrect. Color does not matter as much as relevance and audience understanding. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. Will this image fill the empty space on the slide?#Incorrect. Filling space is decoration, not purposeful communication. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. Can I use this image without mentioning it?#Incorrect. A visual should be connected to the message with explanation or a label. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

::ENG3_U06_L05_GP04::MLA.ENG3.C.02
Context: A student adds a timeline to explain the order of research findings.
Which revision would make the timeline stronger for the audience?{
~A. Remove all labels so the slide looks cleaner#Incorrect. Labels are necessary because the audience needs to understand the sequence. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. Use tiny text to fit every detail from the research notes#Incorrect. Too much small text makes the timeline difficult to read. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=C. Highlight the three dates most connected to the claim#Correct. Selecting the most relevant dates helps the audience focus on information that supports the presentation. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~D. Add unrelated images beside every date#Incorrect. Unrelated images distract from the timeline's purpose. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

::ENG3_U06_L05_GP05::MLA.ENG3.C.02
Context: A student explains, "I used this image because it looks cool."
What is the best revision of that explanation?{
~A. I used this image because every presentation needs at least one picture.#Incorrect. This treats multimedia as decoration instead of communication support. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=B. I used this image because it helps the audience visualize the conflict described in my evidence.#Correct. This explanation connects the multimedia element to audience understanding and evidence. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. I used this image because it was easy to find online.#Incorrect. Ease of finding an image does not show that it improves audience understanding.
~D. I used this image because it takes up space beside my notes.#Incorrect. Filling space is not a strong reason to include multimedia. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}
